WEBVTT

00:53.480 --> 00:56.650
I am Count D.
Welcome to my pet shop.

00:57.390 --> 00:59.080
This is Chinatown.

00:59.450 --> 01:01.450
A mysterious place...

01:01.790 --> 01:05.230
where rare and valuable
commodities are in abundance.

01:06.860 --> 01:11.300
Tonight, you shall find
something you desire.

01:24.880 --> 01:26.140
Welcome.

01:26.680 --> 01:28.670
You must be Mr. Iason Gray.

01:29.320 --> 01:30.220
Yes.

01:30.490 --> 01:33.820
I was told the pet my
wife ordered was here.

01:34.560 --> 01:35.610
Yes...

01:35.820 --> 01:39.490
We finally received the pet
Ms. Evangeline Blue had ordered.

01:39.830 --> 01:42.730
However, due to her accidental
death a few days ago,...

01:43.630 --> 01:47.000
we are not certain
what to do with it.

01:49.170 --> 01:52.160
Where is the pet she ordered?

01:58.480 --> 01:59.810
Please come this way.

02:02.880 --> 02:04.410
What kind of a pet is it?

02:04.850 --> 02:06.720
A dog? A cat?

02:07.190 --> 02:08.450
A fish.

02:08.660 --> 02:12.680
A fish? A tropical fish or is it
a colored carp or something?

02:13.130 --> 02:18.120
No. It's a rather rare species.
We cannot display it in the store.

02:23.510 --> 02:26.100
It's beautiful.

02:29.840 --> 02:31.840
It must be a huge fish.

02:31.910 --> 02:34.140
Please climb up the ladder
and take a look.

02:49.330 --> 02:50.850
I can't see anything.

02:53.230 --> 02:57.190
Such dark water...
Just like the water on that night...

03:07.520 --> 03:08.410
Eva!

03:10.050 --> 03:12.180
Eva! You are alive!

03:12.290 --> 03:12.950
Eva!

03:13.090 --> 03:15.780
Sir, you shouldn't lean out so far.

03:17.290 --> 03:20.280
Please look carefully.
It's a mermaid.

03:21.530 --> 03:22.550
A mermaid?

03:23.400 --> 03:25.390
Eva! It's me! Iason!

03:26.100 --> 03:27.800
Your legs...
What happened to your legs?

03:27.870 --> 03:30.270
What kind of mechanism is that?
Evangeline!

03:30.370 --> 03:31.960
Please calm down, sir.

03:32.470 --> 03:35.810
To tell you the truth,
she was washed ashore...

03:35.940 --> 03:39.780
on the night of the full moon,
last week. I found her by accident.

03:40.650 --> 03:43.340
The night of the full moon?
That was our wedding night!

03:43.950 --> 03:47.290
Look at that ring!
That's the wedding band I gave her!

03:47.620 --> 03:48.490
Is it?

03:48.590 --> 03:51.350
Then, I wonder if she's the
reincarnation of your wife.

03:51.960 --> 03:53.660
The reincarnation?

03:53.830 --> 03:56.160
Well, it may be the
other way around.

03:56.830 --> 04:01.830
In Asia, legend has it that mermaids
live in a palace on the ocean bed,...

04:02.200 --> 04:07.270
and they come to the land sometimes
to mingle with men for fun.

04:08.340 --> 04:15.810
Maybe the Evangeline you married
was a mermaid disguised as a human.

04:16.920 --> 04:18.220
Eva was a mermaid?

04:18.420 --> 04:22.120
Unfortunately, however,
she's lost her memory.

04:22.590 --> 04:27.580
When she came around, she did
not remember where she was from,...

04:27.700 --> 04:32.000
where she was going
or even her own name.

04:34.300 --> 04:36.290
If she recovers her memory,...

04:36.670 --> 04:41.230
maybe she will recall the
pledge she made to you...

04:41.440 --> 04:43.970
and that unfortunate accident.

04:45.550 --> 04:49.710
So, do you like her?

04:50.890 --> 04:53.350
Of course!
I'll take her home.

04:54.020 --> 04:57.890
Then, please sign
this contract.

04:58.860 --> 04:59.660
OK.

05:00.090 --> 05:06.520
Furthermore, sir, please observe
the following sales terms.

05:07.700 --> 05:10.830
(1) Do not let anyone see her.

05:11.440 --> 05:15.770
(2) Keep her in a big water tank
and change the seawater frequently.

05:16.180 --> 05:20.940
(3) Do not let her starve
at any time.

05:21.920 --> 05:23.470
Understood?

05:23.790 --> 05:27.050
In the event that any of these
terms are breached,...

05:27.120 --> 05:31.320
we cannot assume any responsibility
for the consequences.

05:32.190 --> 05:33.920
Understood.

05:34.090 --> 05:37.500
I hope you'll be happy
with her forever.

05:51.010 --> 05:53.500
Eva, how do you like it?

05:54.580 --> 05:56.910
I filled this pool with seawater.

05:59.320 --> 06:00.120
Eva...

06:21.710 --> 06:24.800
Are you really my Eva?

06:28.880 --> 06:30.940
Iason Gray went out last night?

06:31.150 --> 06:34.020
Yeah, the patrolmen saw him.

06:34.690 --> 06:36.680
And where did he go, Jill?

06:37.630 --> 06:38.820
To Chinatown.

06:38.960 --> 06:41.190
What! To his pet shop!

06:41.300 --> 06:43.130
I've had enough of this, Leon!

06:43.230 --> 06:46.130
You know Evangeline Blue's death
is officially filed as an accident!

06:46.530 --> 06:48.760
Iason is just a poor bastard
who lost his newlywed wife.

06:49.040 --> 06:51.030
Yes, I know that, Sarge.

06:51.310 --> 06:54.470
He was Evangeline Blue's manager.
She was his biggest star.

06:54.640 --> 06:57.170
She was the money-tree
of his record company.

06:57.250 --> 06:59.650
Having her alive would've
been more profitable.

07:00.080 --> 07:03.450
He doesn't have any
motive to kill her.

07:04.820 --> 07:07.050
Now, go back to real work.

07:07.820 --> 07:08.950
Yes, sir.

07:11.930 --> 07:13.020
Damn!

07:13.690 --> 07:17.690
Hey, I hear that the Count at
that pet shop has a sweet tooth.

07:18.770 --> 07:20.960
I'll take care of those papers for you.

07:22.000 --> 07:23.730
Tonight's dinner is on me, Jill.

07:25.940 --> 07:27.670
I have not seen you for a while.

07:27.870 --> 07:29.740
I've got a question to ask you.

07:29.940 --> 07:31.470
But here...a little
something for you.

07:31.610 --> 07:35.510
Oh, is this a fruit tart
from Madam C's?!

07:38.590 --> 07:42.820
Iason Gray was here last night.
Don't try to lie to me.

07:43.190 --> 07:45.090
Yes, he was here indeed.

07:45.860 --> 07:50.520
I sold him a pet, with the hope of
consoling him for the loss of his wife.

07:50.930 --> 07:53.530
I know you. You must have
sold him something fishy!

07:54.740 --> 07:59.470
Not at all. Our motto is to sell
"love, dreams and hopes."

08:00.040 --> 08:02.370
So what did you
sell this time, then?

08:03.450 --> 08:04.540
A mermaid.

08:04.750 --> 08:06.740
A mermaid?

08:09.220 --> 08:11.210
You're trying to sidestep again.

08:11.280 --> 08:13.410
Come on! A tropical fish?
A goldfish?

08:13.520 --> 08:15.550
How much did you sell it for?

08:16.060 --> 08:17.850
So you don't trust me?

08:18.020 --> 08:20.760
"...keep her in a big water tank and
change the seawater frequently..."

08:21.000 --> 08:23.830
"...do not let her starve
at any time..."

08:24.100 --> 08:26.090
Anything wrong?

08:26.470 --> 08:28.460
No...No problem.

08:29.070 --> 08:31.630
But, you are a detective of
the homicide department.

08:31.670 --> 08:33.470
Why are you investigating him?

08:33.740 --> 08:36.680
You know he just got
married to Evangeline Blue.

08:36.910 --> 08:40.350
The singer who fell into the ocean
on the day of her wedding.

08:40.620 --> 08:41.840
Right.

08:42.050 --> 08:44.280
On top of that,
her body hasn't been found.

08:44.490 --> 08:46.750
Her accident is still
big news in the press.

08:46.920 --> 08:49.410
But, it wasn't an accident.
It was murder.

08:50.020 --> 08:51.080
A murder?

08:51.290 --> 08:54.890
But, according to Mr. Iason,
Evangeline came onto the deck...

08:55.000 --> 08:59.130
to sober up and slipped
into the water by accident.

08:59.300 --> 09:01.770
I think Iason Gray is lying.

09:04.010 --> 09:05.030
On what grounds?

09:05.110 --> 09:07.540
My instinct as a
smart detective!

09:07.940 --> 09:09.640
The instinct of a wild animal.

09:11.510 --> 09:14.500
Mr. Iason is not the kind
of person to kill others.

09:14.650 --> 09:15.340
What?

09:15.480 --> 09:18.820
He was truly and completely
devastated by the death of his wife.

09:19.250 --> 09:21.240
Are you telling me
it was an accident?

09:21.820 --> 09:23.810
No, my gut feeling is...

09:26.260 --> 09:28.460
Yes, what if he was trying
to protect somebody?

09:29.230 --> 09:31.420
There were Iason and...

09:33.730 --> 09:35.130
Louise Tessen!

09:35.670 --> 09:41.010
Louise was Evangeline Blue's dresser.
She and Iason were past lovers.

09:41.810 --> 09:44.800
However, he fell in love
with the big star, Eva.

09:45.310 --> 09:51.580
Or rather, rumor has it, Eva
seduced and took Iason from Louise.

09:52.150 --> 09:57.020
So, Louise took revenge on the day of
Eva's wedding for stealing her lover.

09:57.290 --> 10:00.160
Iason kept his mouth shut because
he felt guilty for dumping her.

10:00.330 --> 10:01.690
It makes sense.

10:02.130 --> 10:04.030
Where's Louise?

10:04.230 --> 10:06.670
She went back to her hometown
after the accident.

10:07.000 --> 10:09.300
OK, you go check on her!

10:10.400 --> 10:11.200
Eva...

10:16.640 --> 10:17.610
Eva!

10:18.250 --> 10:20.740
Are you really my Eva?

10:22.180 --> 10:24.410
You've really
forgotten about me?

10:34.900 --> 10:35.830
Eva!

10:38.570 --> 10:40.690
Oh, Eva! Yes, I knew it!

10:42.070 --> 10:44.830
That's the voice of
Evangeline Blue!

10:48.380 --> 10:51.000
Eva!
I will never let you go again!

10:51.880 --> 10:53.870
I don't care if you don't
remember anything!

10:54.120 --> 10:56.110
We can start over again!

10:57.050 --> 10:59.580
I love only you.

11:30.520 --> 11:31.580
Eva!

11:39.530 --> 11:41.390
You're singing for me?

11:45.300 --> 11:46.320
Oh, Eva...

11:53.370 --> 11:55.070
You forgive me.

11:59.450 --> 12:01.540
Talk about my instincts.

12:03.320 --> 12:08.650
Well, I was counting on your
so-called wild instincts.

12:09.620 --> 12:12.020
Count!
What are you doing here?!

12:12.390 --> 12:14.220
I wanted to thank you for
the tart the other day.

12:14.260 --> 12:15.960
I brought you some tea.

12:16.300 --> 12:17.660
Brought me some tea?

12:17.800 --> 12:21.130
Listen, civilians aren't
allowed here.

12:21.570 --> 12:22.660
Don't worry.

12:22.740 --> 12:25.800
The Chief of this police department
is a good client of our store.

12:32.410 --> 12:34.970
And, what happened
with Eva's dresser?

12:35.750 --> 12:37.980
Oh, I went to see
her this morning.

12:42.090 --> 12:45.290
I haven't seen Iason
since that accident.

12:46.330 --> 12:51.790
Even if I do marry someone in
the future, it wouldn't be him.

12:53.500 --> 12:55.700
No matter what,
I would never marry him!

12:56.600 --> 12:58.590
Those tears were real.

12:59.740 --> 13:00.970
Were they?

13:01.080 --> 13:06.780
To begin with, what's the difference
between a woman's real and fake tears?

13:08.520 --> 13:13.890
Even a mermaid would shed tears
to get someone she loves.

13:14.790 --> 13:19.120
Fairy tales say that a
mermaid's tears become pearls.

13:20.030 --> 13:23.430
I wonder if some of those tears
would become imitation pearls.

13:24.200 --> 13:26.930
Are you telling me that
Louise is the murderer?

13:27.500 --> 13:30.440
I did not say that.
Please, your tea is getting cold.

13:30.870 --> 13:34.170
Speaking of mermaids,
in Asia, they say you can gain...

13:34.740 --> 13:41.080
eternal youth by consuming the
fresh entrails from a mermaid.

13:42.020 --> 13:44.010
You Chinese actually
eat things like that?

13:45.050 --> 13:46.350
I'm not sure.

13:46.420 --> 13:48.820
Yet, I hear it is such
a great delicacy that,...

13:48.890 --> 13:51.050
once you taste it, you can
never live without it.

13:51.360 --> 13:53.090
Just like human flesh.

13:55.260 --> 13:58.460
Leon, part of Evangeline's body was
found washed up on the shore.

13:59.270 --> 14:00.490
Here's the photo.

14:00.870 --> 14:02.860
It looks as if the body
was torn up by a shark.

14:02.940 --> 14:05.300
It's only the left thigh and it's
already decomposed pretty badly,...

14:05.340 --> 14:07.030
but it must be Eva's.

14:07.780 --> 14:08.670
Leon?

14:11.580 --> 14:13.980
An autopsy has confirmed that the
recently discovered human remains...

14:14.010 --> 14:15.540
are those of Evangeline Blue.

14:15.680 --> 14:18.410
Grieving fans have gathered here,
forming long lines.

14:18.920 --> 14:23.290
We now broadcast a special program as
a tribute to the late Evangeline Blue.

14:23.860 --> 14:29.160
The next request is from her
million selling album in '91 ...

14:56.420 --> 14:57.290
Iason!

14:57.390 --> 14:58.260
Iason!

14:58.330 --> 15:01.020
A detective came to
my house today, Iason!

15:02.300 --> 15:03.280
Iason!

15:06.300 --> 15:07.390
Iason!

15:08.970 --> 15:10.700
Iason, why didn't you
answer the phone?

15:13.070 --> 15:15.060
What's wrong?
You look so pale.

15:15.170 --> 15:18.630
What do you want?
Eva is waiting for me.

15:18.910 --> 15:20.310
Eva is dead!

15:21.450 --> 15:24.970
Listen, you can hear Eva singing.

15:25.790 --> 15:28.310
She only wanted to
scare us a little.

15:28.820 --> 15:33.320
It was one of her usual games.
But it made me realize finally...

15:33.730 --> 15:36.850
who was the most important
woman in my life.

15:37.400 --> 15:39.390
I found true love.

15:47.070 --> 15:50.440
Evangeline is the one I love.

15:56.620 --> 15:57.910
Iason! Open up!

15:58.450 --> 15:59.540
Iason!

15:59.920 --> 16:01.050
Iason!

16:01.450 --> 16:02.580
Iason!

16:03.120 --> 16:04.150
Iason!

16:07.360 --> 16:09.120
Sorry to keep you waiting, Eva.

16:09.930 --> 16:11.860
I will love you forever.

16:42.160 --> 16:44.460
You want to tell us the truth
behind Eva's accident?

16:44.830 --> 16:46.990
Yes, everything.

16:48.500 --> 16:52.900
That night, Iason and I slipped out
from the party to go onto the deck.

16:54.310 --> 16:58.070
Louise, forgive me.
It's all for the company.

16:58.410 --> 16:59.970
I understand.

17:00.650 --> 17:04.610
Eva has had everything she
wanted since she was a child.

17:05.420 --> 17:08.850
Choosing me as her husband
was just one of her whims.

17:09.760 --> 17:11.750
She wanted you because...

17:11.830 --> 17:15.950
you were the only one man around her
who wouldn't fall in love with her.

17:17.460 --> 17:18.490
Louise...

17:22.970 --> 17:26.910
The only one I truly love is you.
My heart is forever yours.

17:32.180 --> 17:33.110
Eva!

17:37.650 --> 17:39.480
Eva, listen...

17:46.730 --> 17:47.820
Eva, wait!

18:04.510 --> 18:08.110
Her scream is still
ringing in my ears.

18:09.180 --> 18:12.520
Iason and I vowed not to tell
anybody about it,...

18:12.890 --> 18:15.620
and not to see each
other ever again.

18:17.590 --> 18:21.490
But, Eva came back as an apparition
to avenge her death on Iason.

18:22.560 --> 18:25.900
When she was alive,
she took Iason away from me.

18:25.930 --> 18:29.330
Now, in her death,
she is going to take Iason's life.

18:30.400 --> 18:34.170
I will bear any punishment.
Please save Iason.

18:34.880 --> 18:39.110
It was a suicide.
My instinct was half right.

18:39.480 --> 18:41.500
Even if Eva killed herself
because of you two,...

18:41.550 --> 18:44.380
it does not constitute a
crime in the legal sense.

18:44.750 --> 18:48.050
Besides, the police
cannot arrest a ghost.

18:48.090 --> 18:50.490
There is no physical evidence.

18:51.260 --> 18:54.250
To help Iason, you'd have to go
to a psychiatrist or therapist.

18:54.530 --> 18:56.520
No, please...!

18:56.860 --> 19:00.030
But, Iason keeps a huge
fish in his pool.

19:00.600 --> 19:03.970
Something the size of
a dolphin or a shark.

19:04.470 --> 19:05.330
A shark?

19:05.570 --> 19:08.510
Iason thinks that fish is Eva.

19:27.860 --> 19:31.300
Count, what did you sell to Iason?!

19:31.800 --> 19:34.200
I already told you,
it was a mermaid.

19:34.930 --> 19:38.500
She is a proud and
possessive creature.

19:39.070 --> 19:43.630
If it helps to get someone she loves,
she will not mind showing her tears.

19:44.180 --> 19:46.740
Just as Eva did that night.

19:47.450 --> 19:48.280
Eva?

19:50.080 --> 19:53.350
By the way, is that
small-minded prince...

19:53.420 --> 19:59.820
who has mistaken guilt for true love
still keeping to the sales terms?

20:00.360 --> 20:01.380
The sales terms?

20:01.590 --> 20:03.590
Not to starve her at any time.

20:04.160 --> 20:06.830
She becomes ferocious
when she is hungry.

20:11.070 --> 20:14.270
Though it may just as well
be what he wanted.

20:16.280 --> 20:17.260
Eva...

20:35.430 --> 20:36.330
Where's the pool?!

20:36.360 --> 20:37.730
The sun room
in the back!

20:41.830 --> 20:43.170
What's that smell?

20:45.570 --> 20:46.730
Turn the lights on!

21:14.600 --> 21:18.470
It's been reported that the skeleton of
the upper torso of Evangeline Blue,...

21:18.570 --> 21:21.040
who fell into the ocean
several days ago....

21:21.110 --> 21:24.410
was discovered inside the
stomach of a strange large fish....

21:24.440 --> 21:26.470
along with the body
of Mr. Iason Gray.

21:44.700 --> 21:47.890
Once tasted, you can
never live without it.

21:48.800 --> 21:52.290
That's the taste of
the delicacy called love.

21:55.640 --> 21:59.630
Mermaids are very
possessive creatures.
